{% comment %}
  snippets/ff-permanent-compare-hidden.liquid

  SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for the French Fitness permanent-comparison-price rule
  (issue #775). Decides whether the *permanent* customer-facing comparison
  pricing must be suppressed for a given product:

    - "Retail Price:" / "MSRP:" / "As high as:" labels
    - the crossed-out permanent reference price
    - the permanent "You save <amount>" badge

  It deliberately does NOT touch:
    - the normal selling price (that stays the primary permanent price);
    - a valid time-limited promotion (Labor Day etc.), which is rendered by
      'labor-day-sale-note' / 'super-sale' and is separately labeled;
    - any underlying data. custom.retail_price, compareAtPrice, pricing
      history, structured source fields and integration/feed data are all left
      intact. This is a presentation-layer rule only, and is reversible by
      unchecking the theme setting below.

  SCOPE: vendor == 'French Fitness'. Verified against the live store: 'French
  Fitness' is the one and only French Fitness vendor value in the product
  vendor list (no 'FrenchFitness' / 'French Fitness Inc' variants), covering
  1,720 products. Non-French-Fitness brands are never affected.

  Unlike 'labor-day-sale-note', this rule is NOT narrowed by product type or
  by promo-exclusion tags: brand scope is about who makes the product, not
  about discount eligibility, so hidden/child products of the brand are in
  scope too.

  If Larianne's brand/vendor confirmation widens the scope (e.g. a second
  vendor spelling, or a brand metafield), change it HERE ONLY and every
  storefront surface follows.

  USAGE — Liquid snippets cannot return values, so capture the output and test
  it. Two lines at the top of the surface, then use the variable inline:

    {%- capture hide_perm_price -%}
      {%- render 'ff-permanent-compare-hidden', product: product -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}

    {% if product.metafields.custom.retail_price != blank and hide_perm_price contains 'false' %}
      ... permanent comparison markup ...
    {% endif %}

  Accepts:
    product (Product) required. Pass whichever product object the surface has
                      (card_product, product_ref, add_on_product, ...).

  Returns the literal string 'true' (suppress) or 'false' (render as before).
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign ff_hide = false

  unless settings.ff_hide_permanent_compare_price == false
    if product.vendor == 'French Fitness'
      assign ff_hide = true
    endif
  endunless

  echo ff_hide
-%}
